IMPORT prelude

-- Central Sikh Gurdwara Board Act 1981 (Singapore) -- who may vote for and sit on the Board (ss 3, 5, 11), terms, casual vacancies
-- and the Treasurer's two-year limit (ss 3(2), 4(1), 6), the quorum and voting at Board meetings and the force of general-meeting
-- resolutions (ss 7, 8), sealing of deeds (s 2(3)), what the Board may do with property and when it needs the members' general
-- meeting first (s 12), the annual accounts and their audit (s 14), members' personal liability (s 15), and serving legal process on
-- the Board (s 17).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1/4/2022), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CSGBA1981.txt. The deposit says the revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including
-- 1 December 2021"; the latest amendment annotated is s 17, "[Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022]". Most other annotations are [6/87].
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0145 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is short (18 sections) and almost all of it is encoded. Not encoded: s 1 (title), s 2(1)-(2)
-- (incorporation), s 9 (powers despite vacancy, beyond a comment), s 10 (minutes), s 13 (bank and use of funds), s 16 (the Board's
-- rule-making power -- no rules made under it were retrieved, so any fee or condition for entry on the Register is unknown), and
-- s 18 (saving of other rights).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Central Sikh Gurdwara Board Act 1981 -- the Board`

§§ `3(1), 3(3), 5 and 11 -- the Register, voting and eligibility`

-- s 5: the Board "shall maintain a register ... containing the names and other particulars of persons who profess the Sikh faith".
-- (Professing the faith is the only condition the Act itself states; s 16(a) lets the Board's rules add conditions, "including the
-- payment of fees". Those rules were not retrieved, so this is a NECESSARY condition only.)
GIVEN `professes the Sikh faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be on the Membership Register under the Act` IF `professes the Sikh faith`

-- s 3(1): members are "elected at an annual general meeting by persons whose names appear on the Membership Register". No
-- citizenship condition is stated for voters.
GIVEN `voter on the Register` IS A BOOLEAN, `voter is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may vote to elect the Board` IF `voter on the Register`

-- s 3(3): "No person shall be elected or appointed as a member of the Board unless he is a citizen of Singapore and his name is on the
-- Membership Register".
-- s 11: no person shall be elected or appointed "or shall continue to hold office" if (a) "he is an undischarged bankrupt or suspends
-- payment to, or makes any arrangement or composition with, his creditors"; (b) "he has been sentenced to imprisonment for a term of
-- not less than 6 months and has not received a free pardon"; or (c) an extraordinary general meeting of Register members has passed
-- a resolution "calling for the removal of such member from office". No time limit on (b) is stated.
GIVEN `is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN, `has an arrangement with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months of imprisonment sentenced` IS A NUMBER, `received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `removal resolution passed at an EGM` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `disqualified under section 11` IF
        `is an undischarged bankrupt`
    OR  `has an arrangement with creditors`
    OR  (`months of imprisonment sentenced` >= 6 AND (NOT `received a free pardon`))
    OR  `removal resolution passed at an EGM`

GIVEN `is a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `is on the Membership Register` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN, `has an arrangement with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months of imprisonment sentenced` IS A NUMBER, `received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `removal resolution passed at an EGM` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be elected or appointed to the Board` IF
        `is a citizen of Singapore`
    AND `is on the Membership Register`
    AND (NOT `disqualified under section 11` `is an undischarged bankrupt` `has an arrangement with creditors`
                 `months of imprisonment sentenced` `received a free pardon` `removal resolution passed at an EGM`)

-- Continuing in office: s 11 says "or shall continue to hold office"; s 3(3) speaks only of being "elected or appointed". Read
-- literally, a sitting member who stops being a citizen or drops off the Register is not removed by the Act (a reading, not a rule
-- the text states; s 6 "otherwise vacates" is not defined).
GIVEN `is a citizen of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `is on the Membership Register` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN, `has an arrangement with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months of imprisonment sentenced` IS A NUMBER, `received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `removal resolution passed at an EGM` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may continue to hold office` IF
    NOT `disqualified under section 11` `is an undischarged bankrupt` `has an arrangement with creditors`
            `months of imprisonment sentenced` `received a free pardon` `removal resolution passed at an EGM`

§§ `3(2), 4(1) and 6 -- terms, the Treasurer and casual vacancies`

-- s 3(2): "Every elected member of the Board shall hold office for a term of 2 years, but may continue in office until the election of
-- his successor in office."
GIVEN `years since election` IS A NUMBER, `successor has been elected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `elected member is still in office` IF
    `years since election` < 2 OR (NOT `successor has been elected`)

-- s 6: if a member "dies, resigns or otherwise vacates his office before the expiry of his term, the remaining members of the Board
-- shall appoint a person to fill the vacancy for the residue of the term for which his predecessor was elected."
GIVEN `years the predecessor served` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `years the appointee serves` IS 2 - `years the predecessor served`

-- s 4(1): the Board elects a President, a Treasurer and a Secretary "from among the members of the Board except that no member of
-- the Board shall hold office as a Treasurer for more than 2 years consecutively."
GIVEN `is a member of the Board` IS A BOOLEAN, `consecutive years as Treasurer at the end of the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may hold office as Treasurer for the period` IF
    `is a member of the Board` AND `consecutive years as Treasurer at the end of the period` <= 2

§§ `7 and 8 -- quorum, Board resolutions and general-meeting resolutions`

-- s 7(1): "At any such meeting 50% of the members present shall form a quorum. No business shall be transacted unless a quorum is
-- present." Read LITERALLY the quorum is a fraction of those PRESENT, not of the Board, so any meeting with someone present has one.
-- (That the drafter meant 50% of the members of the Board is an inference; the text does not say so.) The size of the Board is
-- taken as an argument only to show that it plays no part. s 9: the Board may act "notwithstanding that there shall be any vacancy".
GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `quorum under section 7` IS 0.5 * `members present`

GIVEN `members of the Board` IS A NUMBER, `members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a quorum is present` IF
    `members present` > 0 AND `members present` >= `quorum under section 7` `members present`

-- s 8(2): "Resolutions of the Board shall be in accordance with the votes of the majority of the members present. In the event of an
-- equality of votes, the President of the Board or the person presiding at the meeting shall have a casting vote."
-- (A "majority of the members present" is read as more votes for than against among those voting; abstentions are not modelled.)
GIVEN `members of the Board` IS A NUMBER, `members present` IS A NUMBER, `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER,
      `casting vote is for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board resolution passes` IF
        `a quorum is present` `members of the Board` `members present`
    AND (    `votes for` > `votes against`
         OR (`votes for` = `votes against` AND `casting vote is for`))

-- s 7(2): "Notwithstanding subsection (1), the Board shall be bound by and shall give effect to any resolution that may be passed at
-- any general meeting of persons whose names are on the Membership Register."
GIVEN `passed at a Board meeting` IS A BOOLEAN, `passed at a general meeting of the Register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board must give effect to the resolution` IF
    `passed at a Board meeting` OR `passed at a general meeting of the Register`

§§ `2(3) -- sealing deeds`

-- s 2(3): deeds and instruments requiring the seal "shall be sealed with the common seal of the Board in the presence of the
-- President, the Treasurer and the Secretary of the Board, and shall be signed by the President, the Treasurer and the Secretary".
-- Such signing is "sufficient evidence of the due sealing".
GIVEN `President present and signed` IS A BOOLEAN, `Treasurer present and signed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `Secretary present and signed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deed is duly sealed` IF
    `President present and signed` AND `Treasurer present and signed` AND `Secretary present and signed`

§§ `12 -- property and fund-raising`

-- s 12(a): the Board may "acquire, purchase, lease, hold and enjoy movable and immovable property ... for use in connection with any
-- temple except that the Board shall not exercise such powers in regard to immovable property without a resolution being first
-- passed at a general meeting of persons whose names are on the Membership Register"; (b) the same proviso for selling, mortgaging,
-- demising and otherwise disposing of "any of such property"; (c) "erect such buildings on land belonging to the Board ... as may
-- appear to the Board necessary or desirable for the purposes of any temple" -- with NO general-meeting proviso; (d) "raise funds by
-- means of voluntary subscriptions" for its purposes under the Act.
DECLARE Dealing IS ONE OF
    `buying movable property`
    `buying land`
    `taking a lease of land`
    `selling movable property`
    `selling land`
    `mortgaging land`
    `letting out land`
    `erecting a building on Board land`
    `raising voluntary subscriptions`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `concerns immovable property` IF
    CONSIDER `the dealing`
    WHEN `buying land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `taking a lease of land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `selling land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `mortgaging land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `letting out land` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing, `general meeting resolution passed first` IS A BOOLEAN, `for a temple purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may undertake the dealing` IF
        ((NOT `concerns immovable property` `the dealing`) OR `general meeting resolution passed first`)
    AND CONSIDER `the dealing`
        WHEN `buying movable property` THEN `for a temple purpose`
        WHEN `buying land` THEN `for a temple purpose`
        WHEN `taking a lease of land` THEN `for a temple purpose`
        WHEN `erecting a building on Board land` THEN `for a temple purpose`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `14 -- accounts and audit`

-- s 14(1): the Board "shall at least once in every year prepare an account of the funds and other property of the Board"; (2) "All
-- such accounts shall be signed by the Treasurer of the Board and shall be audited by 2 persons whose names are on the Membership
-- Register and have been elected to serve as such at the biennial general meeting". (Accounts are annual; the auditors are elected
-- at a BIENNIAL meeting. "2 persons" is read as exactly two.)
GIVEN `months since the last account` IS A NUMBER, `signed by the Treasurer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `auditors on the Register and elected at the biennial general meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accounts comply with section 14` IF
        `months since the last account` <= 12
    AND `signed by the Treasurer`
    AND `auditors on the Register and elected at the biennial general meeting` = 2

§§ `15 -- personal liability of members`

-- s 15: "No member of the Board shall be personally liable for or in connection with any act or omission done or committed in good
-- faith and without gross negligence as such member of the Board nor for any debt, liability, act or omission of the Board."
-- The second limb (the Board's own debts) carries no good-faith condition.
GIVEN `claim is for a debt or liability of the Board` IS A BOOLEAN, `acting as a member of the Board` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `grossly negligent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 15 shields the member` IF
        `claim is for a debt or liability of the Board`
    OR  (`acting as a member of the Board` AND `acted in good faith` AND (NOT `grossly negligent`))

§§ `17 -- serving process on the Board`

-- s 17: "Any originating claim or other legal process and any notice may be served on the Board by serving it on an official of the
-- Board or by leaving it at, or sending it by registered post to, the Central Sikh Temple, Singapore." Officials are the President,
-- Treasurer, Secretary and any other officials the Board elects (s 4). The section is permissive ("may"); whether other methods are
-- excluded is not decided here -- the rule says only which methods s 17 itself authorises.
DECLARE ServiceMethod IS ONE OF
    `handing it to the Secretary`
    `handing it to the President`
    `handing it to a Board member who is not an official`
    `leaving it at the Central Sikh Temple`
    `registered post to the Central Sikh Temple`
    `ordinary post to the Central Sikh Temple`
    `registered post to another gurdwara`

GIVEN `the method` IS A ServiceMethod
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 17 authorises the method` IF
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `handing it to the Secretary` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `handing it to the President` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `leaving it at the Central Sikh Temple` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `registered post to the Central Sikh Temple` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
